    <!-- ===== Town of Gludio : services de la ville (rôles des villes de Lineage 2) ===== -->
    <npc id="6b6ab0bc-ff53-430c-bc32-30f330f37f07">
        <name>Gatekeeper</name>
        <title>Gatekeeper</title>
        <type>GATEKEEPER</type>
        <gender>WOMAN</gender>
        <dialogue>
            <greeting>Welcome to Gludio, traveler. The four teleport circles at the end of the roads will carry you wherever the roads go.</greeting>
            <options>
                <label>Where do the teleporters lead?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>North to Gludio Castle, west to the Ruins of Agony, south to the Ruins of Despair, and east, past the river, to the Cruma Marshlands. Dion lies beyond the marsh.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Which places are safe for a beginner?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>Beginners should hurry west along the old road through the Ruins of Agony, to the Forest's Edge beyond: the beasts there are gentle, and the woods further on grow wilder as you grow stronger. Come back to the Ruins of Agony and of Despair around level fifteen; the Cruma Marshlands are for hunters of level twenty-five and more. Stay on the roads: the restless dead attack anyone who strays too close.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Goodbye</label>
                <type>LEAVE</type>
            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>70</level>
    </npc>
    <npc id="6132be62-3c93-4057-8054-75214f3dda20">
        <name>Warehouse Keeper</name>
        <title>Warehouse Keeper</title>
        <type>WAREHOUSE_KEEPER</type>
        <gender>MAN</gender>
        <dialogue>
            <greeting>The Dwarven Guild keeps the town's goods safe. What brings you to my counter?</greeting>
            <options>
                <label>Can I store my belongings here?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>Not yet, friend: the vaults are being rebuilt after the last siege. Come back once the guild has finished its work.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Goodbye</label>
                <type>LEAVE</type>
            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>70</level>
    </npc>
    <npc id="5d3f1aee-8877-4399-bf8f-567b1ad2d242">
        <name>Priest</name>
        <title>Priest of Einhasad</title>
        <type>PRIEST</type>
        <gender>MAN</gender>
        <dialogue>
            <greeting>May the light of Einhasad guide your steps, child.</greeting>
            <options>
                <label>Who is Einhasad?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>The goddess of light, mother of the humans. Her temple watches over Gludio, and her priests bring the fallen back to life.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>The undead in the ruins...</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>The Ruins of Agony and of Despair are cursed ground. Holy magic burns the restless dead: remember it when you walk among them.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Goodbye</label>
                <type>LEAVE</type>
            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>70</level>
    </npc>
    <npc id="7af55075-ef37-485d-a17b-a3ab7982d8bf">
        <name>Townswoman</name>
        <title>Citizen of Gludio</title>
        <gender>WOMAN</gender>
        <dialogue>
            <greeting>Have you seen the statue? They say it honors the hero who drove the orcs from these walls.</greeting>
            <options>
                <label>Any news?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>Merchants from Dion say giant insects roam the Cruma Marshlands again. I would not take the east road alone.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Goodbye</label>
                <type>LEAVE</type>
            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>1</level>
    </npc>
    <npc id="4fb1d6bd-021b-44d2-8226-541c70b3486e">
        <name>Farmer</name>
        <title>Farmer</title>
        <gender>MAN</gender>
        <dialogue>
            <greeting>Mind the crops! It took me all spring to sow these fields.</greeting>
            <options>
                <label>How is the harvest?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>Good, as long as the keltirs from the woods keep away. The castle guards used to hunt them... not anymore.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Goodbye</label>
                <type>LEAVE</type>
            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>1</level>
    </npc>

